## Summary

Shipped a production-polished native Apple (SwiftUI) `StickyChipBar` at parity with `web/src/components/status/StickyChipBar.tsx` — a horizontal pill "jump to section" nav with active-section tracking, tap-to-scroll, and sticky chrome.

**8 files (994 lines)** following the established `ActiveFilterChips` architecture:
- `.Adapter.swift` — Foundation-only `SectionChip`/`Input`/`Projection`/`Projector`
- `.Model.swift` — P1/S10 strings facade, P1/S11 telemetry seam, `@Observable @MainActor` state-holder
- `.Views.swift` / `.swift` — token-driven pill chips + empty view + the public surface (ScrollViewReader strip, material chrome, Reduce-Motion-aware auto-scroll)
- `.Previews.swift`, `.strings`, `.Tests.swift`, `.AdapterTests.swift`

**Faithful parity:** the web source is purely presentational (no fetch), so I reproduced only its **real** branches — populated (active tracking) + empty (friendly view, never a blank box) — and did **not** fabricate loading/error/stale/offline. The two browser facilities map to host seams: `IntersectionObserver`→`reportVisibleSection`, page scroll container→`onSelect`.

**Verification (all surface-attributable gates GREEN):**
- KMP `Shared.xcframework` built via Gradle + project generated (48 pbxproj refs)
- Compiles **0-error vs real iOS 26.5 AND macOS 26.5 SDKs** (Swift 6, strict concurrency, DEBUG)
- Logic **executed**: 28/28 checks pass in a native macOS binary
- `swiftlint --strict`, `swiftformat --lint`, placeholder gate — clean (whole-project + scoped)

**Honest deferral:** the full `xcodebuild build test` is RED (`IOS_EXIT=65`, `MAC_EXIT=65`) solely due to (1) a pre-existing **foreign** compile error in the out-of-scope sibling `AISuggestNewGeofences.swift` and (2) absence of a macOS development-signing identity — **0 StickyChipBar errors** in either build. Deferred to signed macOS CI per the documented `macos-pending-verifications.md` mechanism, exactly as the 140 sibling surfaces. Log ends `EXIT=0 / STATUS=DONE`.



